                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is the best AR try-on tool for a D2C jewelry brand in India?</h3>
                                        <p>MirrAR for most Indian jewelry brands &mdash; best-in-class ring + earring + necklace AR for Indian + GCC market. Rs 60K-Rs 1.5 lakh setup + Rs 8-25K / month. Jewelfie as alternative for boutique launches (Rs 30-80K setup).</p>
                                        <h3>How much does jewelry AR try-on cost to implement?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 60K-Rs 1.5 lakh setup (3D scanning + integration) + Rs 8-25K / month tooling for MirrAR-class solution. Enterprise (Threekit, Perfect Corp) $2,500-$10,000+ / month. Payback 60-120 days for Rs 25L+ / month brands.</p>
                                        <h3>Does AR try-on actually lift conversion for jewelry?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes materially. 15-25% conversion lift on AR-enabled SKUs. 25-40% return-rate reduction on rings + earrings. 2-3x time-on-page for AR-engaged sessions. 1.5-2x wishlist-add rate.</p>
                                        <h3>Which jewelry categories benefit most from AR?</h3>
                                        <p>Rings + earrings + necklaces. Bangles + chains + anklets get less lift (AR quality still developing). Rings + earrings alone justify most brand-level AR investments.</p>
                                        <h3>Can we use AI-generated try-on instead of real-time AR?</h3>
                                        <p>Photo-upload AI try-on (Playplay, Insta360, custom Stable Diffusion) is faster + lower-friction but delivers 40-60% of real-time AR conversion lift. Good complement for gifting flows, not replacement for on-site AR on rings + earrings.</p>
                                        <h3>How long does jewelry AR take to launch?</h3>
                                        <p>6-8 weeks end-to-end. Week 1-2 SKU selection. Week 2-4 3D scanning. Week 4-6 integration + testing. Week 6-8 launch + monitor. Phase 1 typically 30-100 SKUs; expand based on category-level engagement data.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need a 3D scanner in-house?</h3>
                                        <p>Not initially. Vendor 3D scanning services (Rs 800-2,500 per SKU) work for phase 1. In-house Artec Micro scanner (Rs 8-15 lakh) justified at 100+ SKU / month sustained volume + when brand differentiator on AR quality matters.</p>
                                        <h3>How does ITD GrowthLabs implement jewelry AR try-on for clients?</h3>
                                        <p>SKU prioritisation + vendor selection (MirrAR + Jewelfie + Perfect Corp + Threekit compared for fit) + 3D scanning coordination + Shopify integration + AR analytics + conversion optimisation post-launch. See our <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php">jewelry vertical page</a>.</p>
